    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "methods",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "A signal closes at or below EMA225 minus three population residual standard deviations. Upper-half close requires (close − low)/(high − low) at least one half. Cooldown is reapplied after each filter. Score is mean clipped MFE/sigma minus clipped MAE/sigma, each capped at ten. Development selects under frozen support, lower-MAE and MFE-retention criteria; the selected rule is applied unchanged in the later year. Saved approximate 95% ISO-week bootstrap intervals are pointwise, uncorrected for the candidate search."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "2026 YTD had already been viewed in Study 12 and is not a pristine holdout. Sensitivity cells are correlated. Adjusted chart history is retrospective; five-minute OHLC cannot resolve target/stop ordering. Scores and excursion extrema do not model costs, executable exits or profitability."
    },
